WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.735
It's not me who's changed.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.269
It's the left

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.271
who is now made up of a small contingent

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.539
who've gone mental

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.807
and a large contingent

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.809
who refuse to call them out for it.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.445
But I will.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.548
Do you think Democratic politicians

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.950
have changed their views,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.151
or do you think they're just afraid

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.386
of their

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.420
party's activists

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.588
the way that a lot of Republicans

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.455
are afraid of their party's

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.824
activists, the MAGA folks, be.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.926
They're afraid.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.827
They're just afraid.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.896
Yes, I think I think both sides

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.364
I think, again, this

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.266
fought tribes, I think in this country,

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.734
I think there's old school

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.935
liberals and old school

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.104
conservatives, Republicans and Democrats,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.572
the kind of people who used to.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.607
I think that's the majority

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.141
of the country

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.342
like Hillary Clinton and Jeb Bush

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:42.675
or something.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.076
Yeah,

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.010
the kind of people

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.012
who never agreed on a hell of a lot,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.580
but they found ways to work together.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.382
They didn't hate each other.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.417
It wasn't all about

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.018
making liberal tears

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.154
cry and all this stuff and,

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.423
you know, owning and destroying people.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.490
It was just, yeah,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.192
I don't agree with Bob Dole, but,

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.493
you know, we can work together.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.562
We can get a grand bargain,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.097
that kind of stuff.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.299
And so I think that's the majority.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.201
But then you have Trumpers

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:11.071
and then you have jokesters and

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:12.839
you know,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.275
those fringes are not doing this country

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.543
any great favors.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:18.078
If Donald Trump is challenged

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.046
for the nomination,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:20.513
I mean, he's

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.648
obviously already being challenged

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.049
by Governor Haley, Nikki Haley.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.118
And then there's talk of other people

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.519
that Governor DeSantis

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.555
and Mike Pompeo and others,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.023
Vice President Pence.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.224
Do you think any of them

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.492
can take him out?

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.761
No, but I think what they will do

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.329
is ensure him the nomination

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.430
by splitting all the alternate.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.264
Absolutely.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.732
Same thing that happened before. Yeah.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.201
The only way

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.236
Trump doesn't get that nomination

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.940
is if it's just him and the Sanders,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.641
if it's a bunch of people in there,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.509
know they're going to split

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.510
the anti-Trump vote

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.978
because, you know,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.314
Trump has a very hardcore following.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.281
I mean, it's a cult.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.350
And cults don't ever go away.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.651
Look at Christianity.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.187
So I,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.489
I despair about

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.457
that because I think when politicians

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.492
smell the White House,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.427
they don't care about the repercussions

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:08.461
for the country.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.863
They just want to go for it.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.598
Dissent is against Trump,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.033
I think could get it.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:14.801
You know,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.702
somebody said to me

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.803
once, a conservative guy

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.370
said, the thing

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.671
you guys don't understand

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.940
about us is we don't really like Trump.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.808
Now, that doesn't speak

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.575
for all the Trumpers.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.010
He definitely has some real fans.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.844
Oh, sure.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.346
But there's a lot of people

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.780
who voted for him,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.115
and that's their little secret.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.884
We don't like him either.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.051
We just vote for him

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.052
because the stuff

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.722
that you guys are doing on your fringe

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.224
is scarier to us than what he's doing,

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.526
which is saying a lot.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.994
And I'm not quite with them,

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:41.961
but I get it.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:42.295
Yeah,

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.163
I think it's also that

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.597
that he hates

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.399
the same people that they hate,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.101
even if they don't agree. Yes.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:48.768
And they love it

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.770
that he sticks his thumb in their eye.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:51.571
Yeah.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.205
Do you

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.707
do you think that DeSantis is part

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.709
of the old school Republican tribe,

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.912
or do you think he's more of a Trumper

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.014
to point out that's the great question.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.815
I don't know if he's playing a part

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.652
or if that's really him.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.053
You know, he's

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:07.587
the reason he's

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:08.588
so effective is

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.723
he does two things at once.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.659
He can be a real

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.259
old school

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:13.860
Republican

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.795
who just takes care of business,

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:19.199
you know, COVID, the hurricane, stuff

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:19.866
like that.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.368
He just goes about his business.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.571
He doesn't do crazy stuff.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.673
But then when he wants to throw red meat

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.807
to the base,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.576
he's a performance artist

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.510
and he does a lot

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.312
of really outrageous stuff.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.413
But I get it

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.814
that that's where the party is.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.083
If you want a big future in that party,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.718
especially if you want to take on

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.320
Donald Trump,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.487
you got to ride

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.956
both those horses at once.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.390
Everybody keeps saying to me,

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.859
but he has no personality.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:47.994
I don't think people care.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.329
Like a lot of politicians

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.630
don't have personality.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.365
Nixon had no personality.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.967
I mean, I could name some politicians

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.702
who have absolutely no personality.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.036
It's not a prerequisite.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.372
I mean, it's great if you have one.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.807
Like Obama had a great one

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.609
and Kennedy had a great one.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:05.044
But, you know, Biden is not

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:06.379
you know,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.048
I mean, James Brown at the Apollo.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.316
Exactly.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.017
You know,

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:11.584
I mean,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.119
I don't think that's going to hold

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.387
Ron DeSantis back.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.021
You know, it's interesting.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:17.357
I met this couple from Florida,

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:20.326
liberal Democrats, and then they told me

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.394
how much they loved

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.396
Ron DeSantis, really loved him.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.531
And it's for the governance from Florida.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.033
Yeah, they were from Florida.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.102
The people in Florida like

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.902
he won reelection

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.204
with almost 60% of the vote.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.273
Also, while the rest of the country

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.642
was overdoing COVID Florida,

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.210
I was there during COVID.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.746
It was night and day from this place.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.047
And you know,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.049
I am not one who is ever on the page

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.584
with COVID paranoia.

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.085
So I thought it was a breath

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:46.753
of fresh air.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.354
And the people there,

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.789
when they would visit me here,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.790
sometimes they would say,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.991
Oh my God,

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.159
in the middle of the pandemic,

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:53.860
what do you do?

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.295
You people live like this

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.362
and so unnecessary.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.930
We don't live like this. Right.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.598
And it turned out

00:04:58.598 --> 00:04:59.899
a lot of what Ron DeSantis

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.301
did was smarter than what

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.101
the people

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.403
who are criticizing were saying.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.371
I mean, he kept the beaches open.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.173
Yes. You're not going to get it outside.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.541
In fact, it's good.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.509
Get some fresh air

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.209
and some sunshine

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.277
that would be better for you.

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.112
And he also protected the elderly.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.881
It was much more targeted.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.182
It's sort of the opposite

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.550
of what happened in New York State.

